'' A 'wstring * N' element and '(*pw)[ i ]' are 4 bytes on macos-arm64 -- fbc-modern
'' (-target linux-x86_64) writes '*(uint32*)Q$1 = 34u' and '#print typeof( q[0] )' says
'' ULONG. tiko scaled the index by 4 and stored 16 bits, so the upper half kept stack
'' garbage: tiko-rt's fb_WriteWstr ('openq[0] = 34' on an '= any' buffer) printed '?' for
'' WRITE #'s opening quote on linux-arm64. 'pw[ i ] = n' and the '*pw + 0' decay were
'' already right (wchar-width-linux). 'csign( q )' is fb_WstrValInt, untruncated.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target macos-arm64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/wchar-width-fixed.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: %t4 = mul i64 0, 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: store i32 %t7, ptr %t5, align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: %t8 = load i32, ptr %t7, align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: store i32 %t8, ptr %t6, align 4
'' EXPECT-OUT: %t9 = load i32, ptr %t8, align 4
'' EXPECT-NOT: i16
